WEBVTT

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:12.070
This was the most I could afford,
but I hope you like it.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.910
My, whatever could it be?

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.880
Huh?

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.500
Satoko-<i>chan</i>?

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.840
How did you know?

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:40.020
Please! A trapmaster like me
can spot a trap a mile away!

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:58.250
Up until last night,
it <i>was </i>a trap, just as you thought.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.790
But not anymore.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:04.580
I changed it to something that
would make you happy instead.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.710
I'll ask again.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.090
How did you know?

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.980
Whoa!

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.560
Guys, this isn't funny...

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.940
To think <i>this </i>would be my undoing...

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:25.940
Sato--

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:38.200
N-No...!

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.960
HIGURASHI: WHEN THEY CRY SOTSU

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.250
Oh dear, Rika.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.870
Did you have yet another nightmare?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.630
What's wrong?

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.380
A nightmare?! Those weren't nightmares!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.470
They were all real!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.810
And <i>you </i>were--

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.410
I was <i>what</i>?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.410
Are you implying
that I am to blame for this?!

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:32.500
It wasn't me! It wasn't me! It wasn't me!

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.560
It was <i>your fault</i>,...

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:46.600
...Rika!

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.180
You're to blame!

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.430
Why...? Why?!

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.560
You want to know <i>why</i>, Rika?!

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:41.400
It's all because you <i>dreamed</i>
of going to St. Lucia!

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.990
This is all...

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.160
...your fault!

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.240
It's all because of that stupid dream!

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.540
Rika!

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.170
So you hate this place
because it's a "hick town"?

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.800
You want to experience high society?

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:13.520
Why don't you like Hinamizawa?!
What is it you hate?!

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.850
Keiichi-<i>san </i>is here!

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.320
Rena-<i>san </i>is here!

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.320
Mion-<i>san </i>and Shion-<i>san </i>are here,

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.820
and I'm here, too!

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:27.780
You didn't want for anything!
You were happy here!

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.620
Right, Rika?!

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.960
But still, you wanted to
"work hard" to chase that dream?

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:39.130
What's so good about St. Lucia?!

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:40.420
Satoko...

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:45.090
They'd know you're from the boonies!
It's so stupid and boring!

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:47.260
Why do you like it so much, then?!

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:52.770
You said you hated studying, but you'd
work hard to make your dream come true!

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:55.730
You said you wanted to get in with me!

00:06:55.730 --> 00:07:01.360
You said you'd still stick with me!
You'd never leave me by myself!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:16.080
You're a liar, Rika!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.380
You're a filthy liar!

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.800
<i>I'm </i>the liar?

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.920
Th-The hell's goin' on?!

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.340
Hojo! This is blasphemy!

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.180
Satoko-<i>chan</i>?!

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:31.640
Wait, what's going on?!

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.680
This isn't part of the dance, right?

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.600
Of course not!

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.310
What makes me a liar?!

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:42.520
None of what you're saying makes sense!

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.370
It just went up in flames!

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:02.460
--What should we do?!
--What is happening?!

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:05.630
--Water! Get water!
--Someone get a hose!

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:09.760
Mion!

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:14.850
Get out of there, guys!

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:21.020
What's so wrong about wanting
to experience something new?!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.190
Why do you hate that so much?!

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:26.320
You don't want to go
because you hate studying?

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:27.940
Rika-<i>chan</i>?!

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:31.700
If you worked a little harder,
it wouldn't be a problem!

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.250
Oh my God, did Rika-<i>sama </i>just...

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:45.840
You tried to ride a unicycle and get
on stilts, but you could never do it!

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:47.260
That's right. So what?

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.680
It's the same as that!

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.350
No matter how hard I study,
I'll never do well!

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:57.100
Someone, get a teacher!

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:00.890
Because I <i>hate </i>studying!

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.730
I hate it! I hate it!
I hate it! I hate it!

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:06.570
I hate it! I hate it! I hate it <i>so much</i>!

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:12.530
Then I'll <i>make </i>you stay up
later to study harder!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.580
Because going to St. Lucia with you...

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:22.920
...has <i>always </i>been my dream!

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.170
Yes, I know.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:36.640
That's why I went along with it!

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.440
But you abandoned me.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:48.610
When we got to St. Lucia,
you left me all alone!

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:52.650
You promised! You <i>swore </i>you wouldn't!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:12.380
I must've reached out to you <i>dozens</i>
of times while we were there!

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.010
Yes, you did at first!

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:26.730
But then you were far more
interested in the <i>other </i>girls!

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:31.940
I bet it's because you "didn't like them"
and turned down our invitations!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:36.740
I gave you space to spend time
with other people!

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.580
And did I <i>ask </i>you to do that?!

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.620
Stop blaming me for all this!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.040
So because I didn't help you study...

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:54.170
...you failed out of the "good" class,
and it's all my fault?

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:55.760
Yes, obviously!

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:03.350
Because I never fit in there! I only
went there to make your dream come true!

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.650
You should know how to study on your own

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:12.150
by the time you're in high school.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.610
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.450
I <i>hate </i>studying!

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.700
Who cares?!

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.540
I just wanted...

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.680
...to be with you!

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:50.770
Here in Hinamizawa!

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.820
At St. Lucia!

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:56.570
That was all I ever wanted!

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:13.420
Now <i>this </i>is the utmost form of
entertainment, sure to dispel my ennui!

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.350
I would advise that you stop.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:56.380
Whatever were you going to do
after releasing yourself from your bonds?

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:04.100
How could a worthless failure
defeat that from whence she came?

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:07.680
I may possess much that you do not,

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:12.150
but you do not possess
anything that I lack.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:17.780
As such, your defeat
at my hand is <i>certain</i>.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:19.280
Not true.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:23.070
There is one method of achieving victory
in the face of certain defeat.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.240
Oh? What's that?

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.540
A miracle!

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:30.660
As long as the "certain"
can be destroyed by a miracle,

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:34.460
then that which is "certain"
cannot remain "certain" indefinitely!

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:39.090
Show me this "miracle" of yours, then.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:45.140
If you can, then I shall do as you wish.

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:46.760
Rika!

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:50.350
Please, grant <i>me </i>a miracle!

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:57.360
Stop being so stubborn!

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:01.440
Do you know how much trouble
your stubbornness has caused me?!

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.410
What's with this tone
you're taking with me?

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:08.620
What happened to your ridiculous
over-the-top mannerisms?!

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.870
My, don't be a hypocrite.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:14.580
What happened to
that sweet façade of yours?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:19.550
I'm sorry to say,
but this is my true self.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:23.050
You're a looper.
You understand, don't you?

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:25.180
I do indeed.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:29.180
I still can't believe
you have the same power.

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:33.640
It's wonderful.

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:39.900
I <i>love </i>this power!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:43.740
You're just as stubborn as I am!

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.700
I suppose that's true!

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.950
That's why I'll never, ever,

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.660
let you go...

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:57.080
...not in a million years!

00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:12.310
If you <i>are </i>someone who lives in loops...

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:17.850
...then I know what can kill you!

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.870
What are you doing?

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.870
Wha--?!

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.040
Is that--

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:47.050
Onigari-no-Ryuuou. It has the power
to kill one living in loops.

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:50.350
I should have been more careful.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:56.690
This was Hanyuu's last gift...

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:59.310
One I never even wanted!

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:32.100
I don't need that little piece.

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:35.890
So you were the one who took it.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.600
Come now, Rika.

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.440
From this moment forward...

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:54.370
...our <i>real </i>battle begins!

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:11.340
You're not bad, Rika!

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:20.140
This reminds me of that time in club
when a boatload of basins fell atop you!

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:24.360
If you hadn't set a trap for me,
then I would have won!

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.710
No traps today, sadly!

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:45.130
Despite that...

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:51.760
...I will still defeat you!

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:56.100
Club rule #2!

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:02.810
Always strive for victory
with everything you've got!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:06.270
Rika! Quit being such a sore loser, now!

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:09.360
Do you <i>really </i>think you can beat me?

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:12.240
No matter how deep I might
sink into the depths of despair,

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:15.370
or how many dead ends I run into...

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:22.410
...I know that fate <i>can </i>be changed!

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:44.730
Onigari-no-Ryuuou is whole!

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:31.480
Are you witnessing this,
o lesser part of me?

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:37.200
They trifle with a concept no looping
life should: everlasting death!

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:41.030
And they wish to exact it
upon one another!

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:44.790
Yet neither truly wants to kill the other,
and neither wants to be killed!

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:46.710
Why would they?!

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:52.300
Because they want the other to be
with them in their desired world!

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:58.010
What irony! Such foolishness makes
for such wonderous spectacle!

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:05.430
How very entertaining!

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.940
Just give up already!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.900
That's not happening!

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:21.660
How stubborn you are, Rika. In that case,
why don't we <i>both </i>die?

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:23.370
Right here, right now!

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:25.040
Don't be ridiculous!

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:30.210
If that's what you want,
then let's kill everyone else, too!

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:33.800
Let's wipe out everyone else
with a Big Bang

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:38.430
and start the universe over again!
I'd rather have <i>that</i>!

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:50.770
Satoko!

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:01.620
Do it.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:06.450
Erase me from your world.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:13.290
You'll make much fancier friends
at St. Lucia Academy.

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:20.800
That doesn't sound bad.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:23.550
Is she going to kill Satoko?

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:26.010
No, she couldn't kill her!

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:27.640
Whatever will she do?

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:31.810
Perhaps she'll even take her own life!

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:48.410
Is your miracle quite ready yet?

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:58.670
If it is, then use it, quickly.

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:01.300
If not, then disappear.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:10.850
Without a trace, if you please.

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:47.030
Kagurashi-hen:
God-Entertaining Chapter, Part 4

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:46.910
Next time: "Kagurashi-hen:
God-Entertaining Chapter, Part 4."
